      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p00975",
      "unit_index": 1,
      "source_text": "源氏公子看到新生的婴儿，想起古歌",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "Prince Genji looked at the newborn baby and remembered an old poem.",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p00975",
      "unit_index": 2,
      "source_text": "“若非剩有遗孤在，何以追怀逝世人？”",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "If no child were left behind, how could one remember the person who had passed away?",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p00975",
      "unit_index": 3,
      "source_text": "更加泪如泉涌了。",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "At this, his tears flowed even more like a spring.",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p00975",
      "unit_index": 4,
      "source_text": "他想：“这话果然说得是。",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "He thought, This saying is indeed true.",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p00975",
      "unit_index": 5,
      "source_text": "倘使连这个遗孤也没有，更加伤心了。”",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "If even this child left behind did not exist, my grief would be still greater.",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p00975",
      "unit_index": 6,
      "source_text": "这也可聊以自慰。",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "This too gave him a little comfort.",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
